  "result": "I added `click.KeyValue`, exported it from `click`, and added tests. The full test suite passes (1912 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed).\n\n- **Behaviour:** `KeyValue` splits on the first `=`, so `a=b=c` gives `(\"a\", \"b=c\")`. An empty value is allowed (`a=` gives `(\"a\", \"\")`). A missing `=` or an empty key (`abc`, `=value`, `\"\"`) fails with `\"'abc' is not a valid key=value pair.\"`, exit code 2.\n- **Files:** the class is in `src/click/types.py` after `Tuple`, the export is in `src/click/__init__.py`, and the tests are appended to `tests/test_types.py`.\n- **Choices I made:**\n  - The type's name is `\"key=value\"`.\n  - Values that are already tuples are returned unchanged, so tuple defaults still work.\n  - The docstring says `versionadded:: 8.6` because `pyproject.toml` is at 8.5.0. Adjust it if the next release is numbered differently.\n  - I did not add a `CHANGES.md` entry, since that file's top section is already released. Say if you want one.\n\nNothing is committed.",
